                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] I played this on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers and it mostly played fine [/h1]\n\nAnother wave shooter, but I got this game on sale for .59 cents USD.  I think this game is worth at least that much, but not much more.  It could potentially be a great game, but it's very rough around the edges currently playwise.  If the issues are every fixed, it could be a very fun game to play.\n\nThere are locomotion options.  The default is moving by joystick or touchpad, you can also teleport.  There's three different maps (although 2 of them look very similar).   You can move around the map and waves of enemies will come towards you.   Each wave brings more enemies.  You can select weapons from the main menu.  There's actually a decent variety of weapons.  None of them feel polished though.  \n\nI don't think I would recommend this game at $2.99 until issues are fixed.  But this is an easy recommendation at .59 cents if you are interested in another wave shooter, where at least you can move around the map and try different guns.  Just realize, there's a reason why the game is priced so low.  It needs polishing.\n\nSale Price Rating 6/10 ... low expectations were met",
